          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqjw">
            Domestic Violence is an assault that is alleged to have occurred between persons who have a domestic relationship.&nbsp; This charge is pursued vigorously by prosecutors, often despite the wishes of a complaining witness.&nbsp; Domestic Violence charges can range from misdemeanor to felony charges, each carrying not only substantive penalties, but also possible collateral consequences affecting rights to own or possess firearms and the ability of non-citizens to remain in the United States.&nbsp;
          </p>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqjx">
            Those charged with Domestic Violence in Ann Arbor quickly realize how differently these cases are treated by the criminal justice system.&nbsp;Mandatory arrests, swift and severe bond conditions, such as preventing a return to your home or having contact with your significant other or children, are common.
          </p>

          <h2 id="main-1" data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:9gbwg1">Best Ann Arbor Domestic Violence Defense Attorney?</h2>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqkj">
            Attorneys are bound by Rules of Professional Conduct. When advertising, an attorney cannot "compare the lawyers' services with other lawyers' services, unless the comparison can be factually substantiated." <a href="https://www.courts.michigan.gov/4a496f/siteassets/rules-instructions-administrative-orders/rules-of-professional-conduct/michigan-rules-of-professional-conduct.pdf" data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:jbkn7w">MRPC 7.1(c)</a> Simply stated, ethically, lawyers should not be making claims of being "the best" or "#1" or the "top Domestic Violence attorney", as these claims cannot be factually substantiated against their peers. At the Law Offices of Joseph A. Simon, we won't make such boasts and instead rely on our experience, reputation, and peer-review ratings for the highest levels of legal ability and ethical standards. Despite plenty of accolades and case results to support making such claims, we maintain and honor our ethics and let our clients, peers, and case results speak for themselves. We relentlessly pursue excellence in our practice and always strive for the best results for our clients but we will not compromise our ethics to achieve clients by making these boasts as others do.
          </p>

          <h2 id="main-2" data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:9gbwg0">Ann Arbor Domestic Violence FAQs:</h2>

          <h3 data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:o4qtob">My significant other wants to drop the charges. Do I even need a lawyer?</h3>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqkk">
            Ann Arbor Domestic Violence cases are prosecuted by the Washtenaw County Prosecutor's Office in the 15th District Court. The County Prosecutor maintains a "go forward" policy in DV&nbsp;cases, meaning they will pursue and continue prosecution despite any stated desire by a complaining witness to "drop charges." The moving party in an Ann Arbor DV case is the People of the State of Michigan, not the alleged victim. Only the prosecutor, therefore, has authority to dismiss its case. The go forward policy is rooted in the belief that most true victims of domestic assaults will be inclined to protect their batterers and, therefore, require additional guidance and protection. Many police officers, prosecutors, judges and others view domestic violence as a stepping-stone to homicide. An experienced and capable lawyer's intervention is crucial in defending these cases and withstanding the resources of the government.
          </p>

          <h3 data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:o4qtoa">I've been charged with Domestic Violence in Ann Arbor but I didn't start the altercation. Can I press charges too?</h3>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqkl">
            The short answer is "no." The Washtenaw County Prosecuting Attorney won't typically charge both sides of a dispute and once a charging decision has been rendered, it's extremely unlikely to be reversed. But that doesn't mean that conduct can't be used to defend your case. A person is privileged to use reasonable physical force to defend themselves from harm. Moreover, an initial aggressor may not have been truthful to the police at the time their statement was rendered and that could lead to defenses and other legal privileges.
          </p>

          <h3 data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:o4qtno">Is it Best to have a Local Criminal Defense Attorney Represent Me in My Ann Arbor Domestic Violence Case?</h3>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqkm">
            Absolutely. Local, established criminal defense attorneys have an intimate knowledge of the local court practices and participants. Knowing the arguments that will appeal to the presiding judge, knowing the practices and protocols of the local prosecuting attorneys, and having local recognition and standing in a legal community can be invaluable to a case outcome. The Law Offices of Joseph A. Simon is truly local to Ann Arbor. Located in the heart of Ann Arbor, just across the street from Michigan Football Stadium, we regularly and frequently practice in the 15th District Court and stand ready to serve you.
          </p>

          <h3 data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:o4qtnn">What do the best Ann Arbor <a href="/practice-area/domestic-violence-defense" data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:jbkn7x">Domestic Violence Defense Attorneys</a> do to defend a case?</h3>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqkn">
            Ethically, lawyers cannot and should not make claims about themselves such as being “the best.” Instead, lawyers should stand on their experience, ratings, reputation, and results. &nbsp;The best practices for Ann Arbor Domestic Violence defense include: &nbsp;intimate knowledge of the local courts and participants; a thorough confidential client interview; obtaining all case discovery including in-car and body-cam police video, audio dispatch recordings, 9-1-1 audio recordings, interviewing any witnesses, preparing a client for the courtroom, and the ability to present a case in court in pretrial motion hearings and at trial.
          </p>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqko">
            In over 35 years of criminal defense practice, Joseph A. Simon has helped hundreds of people charged with Ann Arbor Domestic Violence charges, aggressively, ethically, and successfully defending these charges and obtaining victories at trial.
          </p>
          <p data-ps="src/pages/practice-area/ann-arbor-domestic-violence.astro:c7mqkp">
            Contact our firm at 734-887-6200 to see why so many people in Ann Arbor have chosen Joseph A. Simon to be their Domestic Violence defense attorney and protect their freedom and reputation.
          </p>
        </article>
